# Playwright artifacts
test-results/
playwright-report/
blob-report/
.playwright/

# Build, dev and audit logs.
#
# None of these belong in version control: they accumulate request paths, uids
# and error strings over time, and `check-no-keys.mjs` scans the tree for leaked
# provider keys — so a log file is exactly the wrong thing to keep around. The
# committed `*.log` files that predate this rule were verified to contain no
# secrets, but the class of file should not have been committed at all.
#
# `lighthouse-report.json` is here for the same reason: a 260KB machine artifact
# regenerated by `npm run lighthouse`.
*.log
lighthouse-report.json

# One-shot extraction/patch scratch output.
#
# `public/webp-extracted/` and `public/webp-assets.zip` are intermediate products
# of an asset pipeline: the committed originals under `assets-source/` and the
# built derivatives under `public/art/` are what the app actually reads.
public/webp-extracted/
public/webp-assets.zip

# Output of `npm run pwa:generate`.
#
# The generator's `dest` values carry a redundant `favicon/` prefix while it joins
# them onto `public/favicon`, so every icon lands one directory too deep. Those
# nested copies are duplicates of files that already exist correctly one level up.
#
# Do NOT "fix" the prefix without reading `generatePWA` first: the same table also
# copies `art/*.webp` sources to `*.png` destinations, so correcting the path
# would replace the committed PNG icons with webp bytes wearing a .png name.
public/favicon/favicon/
public/site.webmanifest